.TH SEED 1 "October 2026" "seed 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
seed \- modern terminal workspace manager, project scaffolder, and health auditor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seed
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seed
is an interactive, keyboard-driven terminal user interface and command-line tool
for organizing development workspaces, scaffolding repositories from built-in and
custom templates, auditing project health, and maintaining file hygiene.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Launch the full-screen interactive Terminal User Interface.
.TP
.B workspace \fR(alias: \fBinit-workspace\fR)
Initialize the standard four-pillar workspace structure: personal/, clients/, resources/, and archive/.
.TP
.B new \fINAME\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Scaffold a new project directory from a template.
.TP
.B check \fR(alias: \fBdoctor\fR) [\fIPATH\fR]
Audit directory health, verify required files, detect junk files, and calculate health score.
.TP
.B sync \fR(alias: \fBmaintain\fR) [\fIPATH\fR]
Repair missing baseline files and clean up temporary or junk files.
.TP
.B archive \fIPATH\fR
Move a completed project into the yearly archive directory.
.TP
.B list
List all available preset and manual templates.
.TP
.B tree [\fIPATH\fR]
Visualize directory structure with file details and human-readable sizes.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell auto-completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell.
.SH KEYBINDINGS (TUI)
.TP
.B S
Cycle project sort order (Recently Modified, Alphabetical, Size, Health).
.TP
.B I / V
Open the selected project in your preferred IDE/editor ($VISUAL, $EDITOR, code, nvim, etc.).
.TP
.B $
Drop into an interactive subshell inside the selected project directory.
.TP
.B E
Open the project README in the in-TUI Markdown editor and previewer.
.TP
.B D
Run health doctor audit on the selected project.
.TP
.B P / T
Display interactive directory tree viewer.
.TP
.B ? / F1
Toggle shortcut cheat sheet.
